-- New York General Business Law, Article 44-B, the Responsible AI Safety and Education
-- (RAISE) Act, as re-added by Chapter 96 of the Laws of 2026: baseline of the frontier
-- developer's questions about critical safety incident reporting.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in
-- New York law has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: a frontier developer (a company), or a developer asking whether it is one.
-- Every input is a fact that developer can state. The rules are in
-- raise-definitions.l4, raise-reporting.l4 and raise-penalty.l4; this module only asks
-- the questions and builds their records. Generated parameter lists are kept identical
-- across questions.
-- Units: computing power in integer or floating-point operations (10^26 is
-- 100000000000000000000000000); money in US dollars; dates in ISO 8601; times as an
-- hour (0-23) and minute in local time with that local time's offset from UTC in whole
-- hours. Both clocks are in HOURS, counted as minutes elapsed on the UTC scale; the
-- start moment is not "day 0" of anything: 72 hours means 4320 minutes after it, and a
-- report at exactly 4320 minutes is in time. No weekend or holiday rule is applied.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `raise-domain`
IMPORT `raise-definitions`
IMPORT `raise-reporting`
IMPORT `raise-penalty`

-- Builds the record of the developer and its model. The revenue field is read only by
-- the large-frontier-developer test; a question that does not ask for revenue passes 0.
GIVEN ai IS A BOOLEAN, broad IS A BOOLEAN, general IS A BOOLEAN, adaptable IS A BOOLEAN
      trained IS A BOOLEAN, used IS A NUMBER, most IS A NUMBER, revenue IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `me and my model`
`the developer and model` ai broad general adaptable trained used most revenue MEANS
    `me and my model` WITH
        `the model is an artificial intelligence model`              IS ai
        `the model was trained on a broad data set`                   IS broad
        `the model is designed for generality of output`              IS general
        `the model is adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks` IS adaptable
        `I have trained, or initiated the training of, the model`     IS trained
        `the operations used to train the model so far`               IS used
        `the most operations I have used or intend to use to train any foundation model I have trained or begun to train` IS most
        `the annual gross revenues of me and my affiliates in the preceding calendar year` IS revenue

-- Builds the record of the incident, in the order of its fields.
GIVEN w IS A BOOLEAN, wh IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `what the model did`, mc IS A BOOLEAN
      single IS A BOOLEAN, people IS A NUMBER, dollars IS A NUMBER, public IS A BOOLEAN
      federal IS A BOOLEAN, loss IS A BOOLEAN, lossh IS A BOOLEAN, dec IS A BOOLEAN
      eval IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the incident as I know it`
`the incident` w wh c mc single people dollars public federal loss lossh dec eval risk MEANS
    `the incident as I know it` WITH
        `there was unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model weights` IS w
        `that access, modification, or exfiltration resulted in death or bodily injury` IS wh
        `the model's conduct`                                                    IS c
        `the model materially contributed to the deaths, injuries, or damage`    IS mc
        `the deaths, injuries, or damage arose from a single incident`           IS single
        `the number of people who died or were seriously injured`               IS people
        `the dollars of damage to, or loss of, property`                         IS dollars
        `the harm came from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model` IS public
        `the harm came from lawful activity of the federal government`           IS federal
        `there was a loss of control of the model`                               IS loss
        `the loss of control caused death or bodily injury`                      IS lossh
        `the model used deceptive techniques against me to subvert my controls or monitoring` IS dec
        `that happened in an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior`        IS eval
        `that behavior demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk`      IS risk

GIVEN d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, off IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `a moment`
`the moment` d h mi off MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `the date`                     IS d
        `the hour`                     IS h
        `the minute`                   IS mi
        `the offset from UTC in hours` IS off

GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, off IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`the moment if` happened d h mi off MEANS
    IF happened THEN JUST (`the moment` d h mi off) ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN det IS A MAYBE `a moment`, rb IS A MAYBE `a moment`, imminent IS A BOOLEAN
      ny IS A BOOLEAN, college IS A BOOLEAN, empire IS A BOOLEAN, declared IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `my reporting position`
`the position` det rb imminent ny college empire declared MEANS
    `my reporting position` WITH
        `when I determined that a critical safety incident occurred`             IS det
        `when I learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred` IS rb
        `I have discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury` IS imminent
        `my declaration of intent under section 1422(9) stands`                  IS declared
        `the model is developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state` IS ny
        `I am an accredited college or university in New York state engaging in academic research regarding AI models` IS college
        `I am the Empire AI consortium or the institute`                         IS empire


§ `Am I a frontier developer, or a large one?`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2), (6), (8), (9)
@export Am I a frontier developer under New York's RAISE Act (Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(8))? Yes if you have trained, or begun to train, a foundation model for which you have used, or intend to use, more than 10^26 operations of computing power.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I a frontier developer` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` MEANS
    `I am a frontier developer` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0)

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(1), (10)
@export Am I a large frontier developer under New York's RAISE Act (Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(10))? Yes if you are a frontier developer and you and your affiliates together had annual gross revenues of more than $500,000,000 in the preceding calendar year.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
      `revenues` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the annual gross revenues, in US dollars, of you and your affiliates (anyone controlling, controlled by, or under common control with you) together, in the preceding calendar year? The test is MORE than $500,000,000.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I a large frontier developer` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `revenues` MEANS
    `I am a large frontier developer` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `revenues`)

§ `Is this a critical safety incident?`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(3), (4) and § 1423
@export Is this event a critical safety incident under New York's RAISE Act (Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4))? Only an event involving a frontier model (a foundation model trained with more than 10^26 operations) can be one, and it must be one of four kinds: (a) unauthorized access to, modification of or exfiltration of model weights resulting in death or bodily injury; (b) harm from the materialization of a catastrophic risk; (c) loss of control causing death or bodily injury; (d) deceptive subversion of the developer's controls outside an evaluation, materially increasing catastrophic risk.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident? The test is MORE than 50.
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, tangible or intangible property did it cause, leaving out any loss of value of equity (§ 1423)? The test is MORE than $1,000,000,000.
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against you, its developer, to subvert your controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is this a critical safety incident` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` MEANS
    `it is a critical safety incident` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0) (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`)

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4)
@export Which kinds of critical safety incident in Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(4)(a) to (d) does this event fit? The list is empty if the model is not a frontier model or no kind fits; an event can fit more than one kind.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident? The test is MORE than 50.
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, tangible or intangible property did it cause, leaving out any loss of value of equity (§ 1423)? The test is MORE than $1,000,000,000.
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against you, its developer, to subvert your controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
GIVETH A LIST OF `a kind of critical safety incident`
`which kinds of critical safety incident is this` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` MEANS
    `the kinds of critical safety incident that apply` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0) (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`)

§ `Must I report, to whom, and by when?`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a), (9); §§ 1425, 1426; L. 2026, ch. 96, §§ 3, 5
@export Must I report this incident to the office within the New York Department of Financial Services under Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a), and by when? Every frontier developer must report a critical safety incident pertaining to one of its frontier models within 72 hours of determining that it occurred, or of learning facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that it occurred: this encoding counts from whichever came FIRST. The answer gives the last moment as the start plus exactly 72 hours, written in the start's UTC offset (a report at exactly 72 hours is in time). No weekend or holiday extension is applied. A clock that started before 1 January 2027 is not covered.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident? The test is MORE than 50.
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, tangible or intangible property did it cause, leaving out any loss of value of equity (§ 1423)? The test is MORE than $1,000,000,000.
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against you, its developer, to subvert your controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
      `determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you determined that a critical safety incident has occurred?
      `determined date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you make that determination (if you have not, give any date; it is ignored)? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `determined hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `determined minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `determined UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
      `reasonable belief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that a critical safety incident has occurred?
      `belief date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you learn those facts (if you have not, give any date; it is ignored)? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `belief hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `belief minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `belief UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
      `New York connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state (§ 1425)?
      `college research` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an accredited college or university in New York state, asking about your academic research regarding AI models (§ 1426(1))?
      `Empire AI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Empire AI consortium or the institute, as defined by Economic Development Law § 361 (§ 1426(2))?
      `federal route declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the office designated a federal law, regulation or guidance document by regulation under § 1422(8), have you declared to the office your intent to comply with § 1422(3) through it (§ 1422(9)(a)), and does that declaration still stand (not revoked by you, and the regulation not revoked by the office)?
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the office`
`must I report this incident to the office, and by when` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` `determined` `determined date` `determined hour` `determined minute` `determined UTC offset` `reasonable belief` `belief date` `belief hour` `belief minute` `belief UTC offset` `New York connection` `college research` `Empire AI` `federal route declared` MEANS
    `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0) (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`) (`the position` (`the moment if` `determined` `determined date` `determined hour` `determined minute` `determined UTC offset`) (`the moment if` `reasonable belief` `belief date` `belief hour` `belief minute` `belief UTC offset`) FALSE `New York connection` `college research` `Empire AI` `federal route declared`)

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a)
@export Did I report my critical safety incident to the New York DFS office within 72 hours under Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a)? Elapsed time is counted in minutes on the UTC scale from whichever came first, your determination that a critical safety incident occurred or your learning facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred, to your report. Exactly 72 hours 0 minutes is within 72 hours; 72 hours 1 minute is not. If neither has happened, the answer is no (no clock has started, so there is nothing to have been in time for).
GIVEN `determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you determined that a critical safety incident has occurred?
      `determined date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you make that determination (if you have not, give any date; it is ignored)? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `determined hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `determined minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `determined UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
      `reasonable belief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that a critical safety incident has occurred?
      `belief date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you learn those facts (if you have not, give any date; it is ignored)? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `belief hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `belief minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `belief UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
      `report date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you report the incident to the office? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `report hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `report minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `report UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`did I report to the office within 72 hours` `determined` `determined date` `determined hour` `determined minute` `determined UTC offset` `reasonable belief` `belief date` `belief hour` `belief minute` `belief UTC offset` `report date` `report hour` `report minute` `report UTC offset` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the moment my 72-hour clock started` (`the position` (`the moment if` `determined` `determined date` `determined hour` `determined minute` `determined UTC offset`) (`the moment if` `reasonable belief` `belief date` `belief hour` `belief minute` `belief UTC offset`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST t THEN `I reported within 72 hours` t (`the moment` `report date` `report hour` `report minute` `report UTC offset`)

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b), (9); §§ 1425, 1426
@export Must I disclose this incident within 24 hours under Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b)? A frontier developer that discovers that a critical safety incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury must disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction. This does not replace the 72-hour report to the office.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
      `weights compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model's weights?
      `weights harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that access, modification or exfiltration result in death or bodily injury?
      `conduct` IS A `what the model did` @desc Did the model do one of these? One of: none of the three kinds of conduct; provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon; engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human; evaded the control of its frontier developer or user.
      `materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model materially contribute to the deaths, serious injuries or property damage below?
      `single incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those deaths, injuries or damage arise from a single incident?
      `people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people died or were seriously injured in that incident? The test is MORE than 50.
      `dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of damage to, or loss of, tangible or intangible property did it cause, leaving out any loss of value of equity (§ 1423)? The test is MORE than $1,000,000,000.
      `publicly accessible information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model?
      `lawful federal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from lawful activity of the federal government?
      `loss of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a loss of control of the model?
      `loss of control harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss of control cause death or bodily injury?
      `deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the model use deceptive techniques against you, its developer, to subvert your controls or monitoring?
      `in an evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that happen within an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior?
      `materially increased risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a manner that demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk?
      `imminent risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury? The 24 hours run from that discovery.
      `New York connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state (§ 1425)?
      `college research` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an accredited college or university in New York state, asking about your academic research regarding AI models (§ 1426(1))?
      `Empire AI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Empire AI consortium or the institute, as defined by Economic Development Law § 361 (§ 1426(2))?
      `federal route declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the office designated a federal law, regulation or guidance document by regulation under § 1422(8), have you declared to the office your intent to comply with § 1422(3) through it (§ 1422(9)(a)), and does that declaration still stand (not revoked by you, and the regulation not revoked by the office)?
GIVETH A `my duty to disclose within 24 hours`
`must I disclose this incident within 24 hours` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk` `imminent risk` `New York connection` `college research` `Empire AI` `federal route declared` MEANS
    `my duty to disclose under 1422(3)(b)` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` 0) (`the incident` `weights compromised` `weights harm` `conduct` `materially contributed` `single incident` `people` `dollars` `publicly accessible information` `lawful federal activity` `loss of control` `loss of control harm` `deception` `in an evaluation` `materially increased risk`) (`the position` NOTHING NOTHING `imminent risk` `New York connection` `college research` `Empire AI` `federal route declared`)

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b)
@export Did I disclose an imminent-risk critical safety incident within 24 hours under Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b)? Elapsed time is counted in minutes on the UTC scale from your discovery that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury to your disclosure. Exactly 24 hours 0 minutes is within 24 hours; 24 hours 1 minute is not.
GIVEN `discovery date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you discover that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `discovery hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `discovery minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `discovery UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
      `disclosure date` IS A DATE @desc On what calendar date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-13) did you disclose the incident to an appropriate authority? Give the date in the local time whose UTC offset you give below.
      `disclosure hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23, 24-hour clock, local time)?
      `disclosure minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute of that hour (0 to 59)?
      `disclosure UTC offset` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that local time's offset from UTC, in whole hours? New York: -5 on Eastern Standard Time, -4 on Eastern Daylight Time (in 2027, daylight time runs from 14 March to 7 November). Elapsed time is counted on the UTC scale, so a daylight-saving change counts as the hours that really passed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`did I disclose within 24 hours` `discovery date` `discovery hour` `discovery minute` `discovery UTC offset` `disclosure date` `disclosure hour` `disclosure minute` `disclosure UTC offset` MEANS
    `I disclosed within 24 hours` (`the moment` `discovery date` `discovery hour` `discovery minute` `discovery UTC offset`) (`the moment` `disclosure date` `disclosure hour` `disclosure minute` `disclosure UTC offset`)

§ `My report: contents, amendments, confidentiality, and other regimes`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(1)
@export What must my critical safety incident report to the New York DFS office give, under Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(1)? The four things the office's reporting mechanism includes. The one input is not used; it is there because a question needs one.
GIVEN `anything` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Unused: answer yes or no.
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of a critical safety incident report`
`what must my report give` `anything` MEANS
    `what my report gives`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(c)
@export May I file an amended report under Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(c)? Yes if you discover information about the critical safety incident after filing the initial report.
GIVEN `initial report filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the initial report required by § 1422(3)?
      `later information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you discover information about the incident after filing it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may I file an amended report` `initial report filed` `later information` MEANS
    `I may file an amended report` `initial report filed` `later information`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(6)
@export Is my critical safety incident report exempt from disclosure under New York's Freedom of Information Law (Public Officers Law, article 6)? Yes for a report submitted to the office under § 1422 (Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(6)).
GIVEN `submitted to the office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit the report to the office under § 1422?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my report exempt from FOIL` `submitted to the office` MEANS
    `my report is exempt from disclosure under FOIL` `submitted to the office`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(8), (9)
@export Does complying with another regime count as complying with New York's 72-hour and 24-hour reporting duties (Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3))? Only one route is in the article: a federal law, regulation or guidance document the office has designated by regulation, after you declare your intent to the office. Compliance with another state's law, such as California's SB 53, is not made to count by anything in Article 44-B.
GIVEN `federal route declared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the office designated a federal law, regulation or guidance document by regulation under § 1422(8), have you declared to the office your intent to comply with § 1422(3) through it (§ 1422(9)(a)), and does that declaration still stand (not revoked by you, and the regulation not revoked by the office)?
GIVETH A `what other compliance counts for`
`does complying with another regime count` `federal route declared` MEANS
    `what complying elsewhere counts for` `federal route declared`

§ `What can happen to me if I don't?`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1427
@export What is the most the New York Attorney General can recover from me for this failure under Gen. Bus. Law § 1427? Only a large frontier developer is subject to it: up to $1,000,000 for a first violation and up to $3,000,000 per subsequent violation, set by severity; there is no private right of action. Whether § 1427 reaches a failed 24-hour disclosure is not plain, and the answer says so.
GIVEN `is it an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from its input how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments (an "artificial intelligence model", Gen. Bus. Law § 1420(2))?
      `broad data set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the model trained on a broad data set?
      `generality of output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model designed for generality of output?
      `adaptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks?
      `did I train it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you trained this model, or initiated its training?
      `operations used so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How many integer or floating-point operations of computing power have been used to train this model so far, counting the original training run and any fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other material modification you applied? (10^26 = 100000000000000000000000000; the test is MORE than 10^26.)
      `most operations on any foundation model` IS A NUMBER @desc Over every foundation model you have trained or begun to train (this one included), what is the largest number of operations you have used, or intend to use, to train one of them? Count the original run and later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning and material modifications.
      `revenues` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the annual gross revenues, in US dollars, of you and your affiliates (anyone controlling, controlled by, or under common control with you) together, in the preceding calendar year? The test is MORE than $500,000,000.
      `failure` IS A `a failure of mine` @desc What did you fail to do? One of: I failed to report a critical safety incident to the office within 72 hours; I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours.
      `first violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your first violation of Article 44-B? The article does not say how violations are counted.
GIVETH A `what I can be made to pay for the failure`
`what is the most the Attorney General can recover for this failure` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `revenues` `failure` `first violation` MEANS
    `what I can be made to pay under section 1427` (`the developer and model` `is it an AI model` `broad data set` `generality of output` `adaptable` `did I train it` `operations used so far` `most operations on any foundation model` `revenues`) `failure` `first violation`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1428(5)
@export What is the most the New York DFS office may levy on me, after notice and hearing, under Gen. Bus. Law § 1428(5), for developing, deploying or operating a large frontier model in part in New York without a current disclosure statement, or with false information in it, or for not paying an assessment? $1,000 for each day of failing to file or to correct false information, plus an amount equal to the assessments owed; this is in addition to any other penalty.
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days have you failed to file the disclosure statement, or to correct false information in it?
      `assessments owed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many US dollars of assessments under § 1428(4) do you owe?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what is the most the office may levy for a missing disclosure statement` `days` `assessments owed` MEANS
    `the most the office may levy under section 1428(5)` `days` `assessments owed`
